<Project>

  <!--
    Prevent the git commit SHA from being embedded in build output.

    The .NET SDK, by default, does two independent things that stamp the current commit
    into every project's assembly bytes:

      1. IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion (default true) appends "+<sha>" to
         AssemblyInformationalVersionAttribute.
      2. Implicit SourceLink auto-import (controlled by SuppressImplicitGitSourceLink,
         effectively false/unset by default even with zero Microsoft.SourceLink.* package
         references) generates obj/**/<Project>.sourcelink.json embedding the commit SHA in
         a raw.githubusercontent.com URL. That file is embedded in the portable PDB, which
         changes the PDB's content/GUID, which is reflected back into the DLL's own Debug
         Directory (CodeView) entry — so the DLL's bytes change even though DebugType is
         "portable" (a separate .pdb file, not embedded in the DLL itself).

    RunnerFingerprint.ComputeContentHash (AlRunner/Infrastructure/RunnerFingerprint.cs) is a
    whole-file SHA-256 of al-runner.dll, stamped into every runner-owned cache key. Left
    unchecked, both behaviors above make that hash a hash of the *commit*, not of the
    runner's *code* — invalidating every cache on every commit, including commits that touch
    only docs or CI config. See issue #1881.

    Both properties are required together — disabling only #1 still leaves the SourceLink
    auto-import changing the DLL's debug-directory bytes across commits.

    Nothing in this repo reads the informational version at runtime: al-runner's version
    flag reports Assembly.GetName().Version (AssemblyVersion, e.g. "2.0.0.0"), not the
    informational version.

    DO NOT DELETE THESE AS "REDUNDANT" IF YOU SEE THEM OVERRIDDEN ELSEWHERE. The published
    NuGet package (publish.yml's `dotnet pack AlRunner/`, PackAsTool=true, pushed to
    nuget.org as MSDyn365BC.AL.Runner) deliberately turns BOTH properties back on at pack
    time (`-p:SuppressImplicitGitSourceLink=false -p:IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion=true`)
    so released packages keep real commit provenance (nuspec RepositoryUrl/RepositoryCommit)
    and source-stepping for consumers. That override is safe and intentional — not because
    the released al-runner.dll is exempt from RunnerFingerprint.ContentHash-keyed caching
    (PackAsTool=true means it's exactly what end users run, and an ordinary run hashes it at
    all three ComputeContentHash call sites like any other build), but because a released
    package's bytes are fixed for a given version, so the ContentHash an end user's run
    computes from it is stable. Commit-embedding only invalidates caches when the SAME code
    is rebuilt commit-to-commit — the dev/CI/test-matrix path, never the release path — so
    re-enabling both properties here cannot reintroduce the #1881 cache-invalidation bug.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion>false</IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion>
    <SuppressImplicitGitSourceLink>true</SuppressImplicitGitSourceLink>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
